# I'm Okay - Agent Development Rules

## Project Overview

Safety check-in mobile app for dependents (elderly, medically vulnerable, children). Dependents confirm wellbeing with a single button press; guardians are notified of check-ins and alerted if one is missed.

**Key Documents:**
- [Product Requirements Document](docs/PRD.md)
- [Design System](docs/design-system.md)
- [Design Assets](docs/designs/)

## Technology Stack

- **Mobile**: Expo SDK (with expo-dev-client), React Native, TypeScript
- **Backend**: Supabase (PostgreSQL, Auth, Storage, Edge Functions)
- **State**: React Context + Zustand
- **Navigation**: Expo Router (file-based routing)
- **Subscriptions**: RevenueCat
- **SMS**: Twilio (premium feature)

## Project Structure

```
/app                    # Expo Router screens (file-based routing)
  /(auth)               # Login, signup, onboarding
  /(dependent)          # Dependent-only screens
  /(guardian)           # Guardian-only screens
  /(shared)             # Both roles
/modules                # Native modules (expo-modules-core)
  /lock-screen-widget/  # iOS WidgetKit + Android App Widget
/components             # Reusable UI components
/lib                    # Utilities, Supabase client, helpers
/hooks                  # Custom React hooks
/types                  # TypeScript type definitions
/constants              # App-wide constants, theme config
/assets                 # Images, fonts, static files
/supabase/functions     # Edge Functions
/docs                   # PRD, design system, design assets
```

## Code Standards

- TypeScript strict mode required - no `any` types without justification
- Functional components with hooks only (no class components)
- Named exports for components, default exports for screens
- Use `StyleSheet.create()` for styles, not inline style objects
- Brief JSDoc comments for complex functions

## Mobile-Specific Requirements

- Always wrap screens with SafeAreaView or useSafeAreaInsets
- Test changes on both iOS and Android simulators before completion
- Use responsive sizing (percentages, flex) - avoid hard-coded pixels
- Implement KeyboardAvoidingView for all form screens
- Every async operation needs loading and error states
- Handle offline scenarios gracefully
- **Minimum touch target: 48x48pt** (critical for elderly users)

## Lock Screen Widget (MVP Core Feature)

The "I'm Okay" button must be accessible from the device lock screen.

- **iOS**: WidgetKit (Swift) in `/modules/lock-screen-widget/ios/`
- **Android**: App Widget (Kotlin) in `/modules/lock-screen-widget/android/`
- Requires `expo-dev-client` - cannot use Expo Go for widget testing
- Widget must update after successful check-in

## Supabase Integration

- Single client instance at `/lib/supabase.ts`
- Generate and use typed client from database schema
- Row Level Security (RLS) policies required for ALL tables
- Handle auth state changes in a global provider
- Use Supabase Edge Functions for server-side logic
- Use pg_cron for scheduled tasks (missed check-in detection)

## Security Rules

- NEVER commit `.env` files, API keys, or secrets
- Validate all user inputs on both client and server (RLS)
- Never trust client-side validation alone
- Store sensitive data in secure storage, not AsyncStorage

## Design References

- **Design System**: See [docs/design-system.md](docs/design-system.md)
- **Color Palette**: Primary `#4CAF50`, Danger `#E57373`, Accent `#7FBFF2`
- **Reference Apps**: Life360, Calm, Apple Health
